 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "<p>“The Columbian Exchange has included man, and he has changed the Old and New Worlds sometimes inadvertently, sometimes intentionally, often brutally. It is possible that he and the plants and animals he brings with him have caused the extinction of more species of life forms in the last four hundred years than the usual processes of evolution might kill off in a million. . . . </p>\n<p>The Columbian Exchange has left us with not a richer but a more impoverished genetic pool. We, all of the life on this planet, are the less for Columbus, and the impoverishment will increase.”</p>\n<p align=\"right\">Alfred Crosby, <i>The Columbian Exchange: Biological and Cultural Consequences of 1492</i></p>\n<p><i>Refer to the excerpt provided.</i></p>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 614559,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Which of the following most directly supports Crosby’s argument?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1166209,
     "content_html": "Population gain in Europe due to New World crops such as the potato"
    },
    {
     "id": 1166210,
     "content_html": "Population decline in North America due to diseases such as smallpox"
    },
    {
     "id": 1166208,
     "content_html": "Mass migration of Europeans to North America in the sixteenth century, displacing Native American groups"
    },
    {
     "id": 1166207,
     "content_html": "Overgrazing by animals introduced by Europeans"
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 614560,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "A historian seeking to discredit Crosby’s argument might use what evidence?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1166213,
     "content_html": "The immediate and widespread adoption of Christianity in the New World\n"
    },
    {
     "id": 1166212,
     "content_html": "Native Americans’ struggles with Europeans for dominance in the New World \n"
    },
    {
     "id": 1166211,
     "content_html": "Native American groups’ failed adoption of European technologies \n"
    },
    {
     "id": 1166214,
     "content_html": "A net population gain over time due to increased availability of high-caloric foods native to the New World\n"
    }
   ],
